IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `g8-fees-nouns`

-- g8-fees-draft.l4: the SimpLEX draft of the Fees Regulations, as Figure 4 of Schwartz, Bar-Siman-Tov and Gelbard
-- (2025) shows it.  The draft exists ONLY as a screenshot (inputs/fig4-simplex-screenshot.png, and the 400 dpi crop
-- of page 386 of the Hebrew paper, inputs/fig4-page34-400dpi.png).  Its Hebrew is therefore not quoted: nothing here
-- is copied from a text file, and no Hebrew is typed.  Every English line below is a description of what the image
-- shows, read at the resolution the image has; a word that the image does not settle is said not to be settled.
--
-- WHAT IS VISIBLE: the title (a draft of the Fees Regulations 5785-2025), the preamble, the heading "Chapter A:
-- purpose and definitions", regulation 1 with two definitions, "Chapter B: fees", regulation 2 with five
-- sub-regulations, and the heading of regulation 3, "update of fees".  The pane then ends.
-- WHAT IS NOT VISIBLE: the text of regulations 3, 4 and 5.  This vintage is therefore SILENT on them by
-- construction: each is a named refusal below, never a figure or a rule borrowed from the as-made text.
--
-- The draft was never in force.  `the day the stated amount took effect` is NOTHING for every fee it states.

§ `The SimpLEX draft of the Fees Regulations (Figure 4, screenshot only)`

§§ `The preamble, the chapter headings and regulation 1 (inert, with one rule for the definitions)`

-- Preamble, as the image reads (inert; no rule turns on it):
--   * it cites section 59 of the Law ALONE (the enacted preamble cites ss.59 and 60);
--   * it says the regulations are made "after consultation with the Minister of Finance and with his approval"
--     under a section of the Budget Principles Law that the image prints as section 139 (the enacted text cites
--     section 39B of that Law and says "with the approval of the Minister of Finance" only: no consultation);
--   * it adds the approval of the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee.
-- Chapter A is headed "purpose and definitions" (the enacted heading is "definitions").
-- Regulation 1 of the draft defines "theoretical exam" first and "practical exam" second.
-- The draft's definition of practical exam speaks of the knowledge and skills "of the student", where the
-- enacted definition speaks of "a learner in a vocational training course".  The image does not settle whether
-- the theoretical-exam definition names the same learner; the encoding takes the same four limbs for both and
-- registers the point as a fork in FRAGMENT-G8.md.

-- The two definitions as one test each over an exam's facts.  Four limbs, as in the enacted definitions.
@ref SimpLEX draft (Figure 4), regulation 1, "practical exam"
GIVEN exam IS AN `Exam in a vocational training course`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the SimpLEX draft, regulation 1 — the exam is a practical exam` exam MEANS
        exam's `assesses the practical knowledge and skills of the learner`
    ... exam's `taken by a learner in a vocational training course`
    ... exam's `on subjects in the curriculum for the installation and service of cooling facilities`

@ref SimpLEX draft (Figure 4), regulation 1, "theoretical exam"
GIVEN exam IS AN `Exam in a vocational training course`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the SimpLEX draft, regulation 1 — the exam is a theoretical exam` exam MEANS
        exam's `assesses the knowledge and deep understanding of the learner in theoretical subjects`
    ... exam's `taken by a learner in a vocational training course`
    ... exam's `on subjects in the curriculum for the installation and service of cooling facilities`

§§ `Regulation 2: fees`

-- The draft's regulation 2 is sub-regulations (a) to (e), numbered with Hebrew letters, no payer named in any of
-- them (the sentences are passive: a payment of a fee of so many new shekels).  As the image reads:
--   (a) for a theoretical exam, a fee of NIS 273;
--   (b) for a practical exam, a fee of NIS 194;
--   (c) where an APPEAL is lodged on "the exam, theoretical or practical" (the draft's word is appeal, the enacted
--       word is objection), NIS 40 per appeal is added to the payment of the fee "as stated in sub-section (a)";
--   (d) for an APPLICATION to receive a licence or to renew it, under section 5 of the Law, NIS 284;
--   (e) for an application to receive a temporary licence for a foreign expert or to renew it, under "section 8"
--       of the Law, NIS 398.
-- Four things to read before the rules:
--   (1) (a) is the THEORETICAL fee, so (c)'s cross-reference to (a) points at the theoretical fee even where the
--       appeal concerns the practical exam; that is a defect of the draft (fork, FRAGMENT-G8.md).
--   (2) (d) prices the APPLICATION; the text as made prices the RECEIPT of the licence (reg.2(c)).  The two
--       vintages therefore price different heads of section 59 and answer silence for each other's head.
--   (3) (e) cites section 8 of the Law; in the enacted Law section 8 is the validity of a licence and the
--       temporary licence is section 9 (trap T35).  The encoding keeps the draft's citation in a comment and
--       attaches the fee to the temporary licence, which is what (e) is about.
--   (4) The amounts are printed with no note; the "adjusted to" notes are the wiki editor's, on the enacted text.

@ref SimpLEX draft (Figure 4), regulation 2(a)
GIVETH A `Fee stated in a vintage`
`the SimpLEX draft, regulation 2(a) — the fee for a theoretical exam` MEANS
    `Fee stated in a vintage` WITH
        `the amount stated` IS 273
        `the provision that states it` IS "2(a)"
        `the payer the provision names` IS NOTHING
        `the day the stated amount took effect` IS NOTHING
        `an objection charge rather than a fee` IS FALSE

@ref SimpLEX draft (Figure 4), regulation 2(b)
GIVETH A `Fee stated in a vintage`
`the SimpLEX draft, regulation 2(b) — the fee for a practical exam` MEANS
    `Fee stated in a vintage` WITH
        `the amount stated` IS 194
        `the provision that states it` IS "2(b)"
        `the payer the provision names` IS NOTHING
        `the day the stated amount took effect` IS NOTHING
        `an objection charge rather than a fee` IS FALSE

-- (c): one provision for an objection to either exam.  The amount printed is NIS 40 per appeal; whether it is
-- the whole charge or an addition to the exam fee is the fork carried by `Reading of the objection charge`.
@ref SimpLEX draft (Figure 4), regulation 2(c)
GIVETH A `Fee stated in a vintage`
`the SimpLEX draft, regulation 2(c) — the charge for an appeal on the exam` MEANS
    `Fee stated in a vintage` WITH
        `the amount stated` IS 40
        `the provision that states it` IS "2(c)"
        `the payer the provision names` IS NOTHING
        `the day the stated amount took effect` IS NOTHING
        `an objection charge rather than a fee` IS TRUE

@ref SimpLEX draft (Figure 4), regulation 2(d)
GIVETH A `Fee stated in a vintage`
`the SimpLEX draft, regulation 2(d) — the fee for an application for a licence or its renewal` MEANS
    `Fee stated in a vintage` WITH
        `the amount stated` IS 284
        `the provision that states it` IS "2(d)"
        `the payer the provision names` IS NOTHING
        `the day the stated amount took effect` IS NOTHING
        `an objection charge rather than a fee` IS FALSE

@ref SimpLEX draft (Figure 4), regulation 2(e)
GIVETH A `Fee stated in a vintage`
`the SimpLEX draft, regulation 2(e) — the fee for an application for a foreign expert's temporary licence or its renewal` MEANS
    `Fee stated in a vintage` WITH
        `the amount stated` IS 398
        `the provision that states it` IS "2(e)"
        `the payer the provision names` IS NOTHING
        `the day the stated amount took effect` IS NOTHING
        `an objection charge rather than a fee` IS FALSE

-- What the draft states for each head of section 59; a head the draft does not price answers NOTHING, and the
-- answer is silence, not a figure from the text as made.
@ref SimpLEX draft (Figure 4), regulation 2(a) to (e); Law s.59
GIVEN service IS A `Service under the Fees Regulations`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Fee stated in a vintage`
`the SimpLEX draft states, for the service` service MEANS
    CONSIDER service
    WHEN `the service of filing an application for a licence or its renewal`
        THEN JUST `the SimpLEX draft, regulation 2(d) — the fee for an application for a licence or its renewal`
    WHEN `the service of receiving a licence or its renewal` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `the service of filing an application for a foreign expert's temporary licence or its renewal`
        THEN JUST `the SimpLEX draft, regulation 2(e) — the fee for an application for a foreign expert's temporary licence or its renewal`
    WHEN `the service of being granted a foreign expert's temporary licence` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `the service of sitting a practical exam`
        THEN JUST `the SimpLEX draft, regulation 2(b) — the fee for a practical exam`
    WHEN `the service of sitting a theoretical exam`
        THEN JUST `the SimpLEX draft, regulation 2(a) — the fee for a theoretical exam`
    WHEN `the service of objecting to the score of a practical exam`
        THEN JUST `the SimpLEX draft, regulation 2(c) — the charge for an appeal on the exam`
    WHEN `the service of objecting to the score of a theoretical exam`
        THEN JUST `the SimpLEX draft, regulation 2(c) — the charge for an appeal on the exam`
    WHEN `the service of attending a continuing training course` THEN NOTHING

§§ `Regulations 3, 4 and 5: not visible`

-- One named refusal for each regulation the screenshot does not show.  Each is returned, never stored, by the
-- functions in g8-fees.l4 that would otherwise have to read the regulation.

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the SimpLEX draft's regulation 3, update of fees, is not visible in the screenshot, which ends at its heading` MEANS
    REFUSE "the SimpLEX draft's regulation 3, update of fees, is not visible in the screenshot, which ends at its heading"

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the SimpLEX draft's regulation 4 is not visible in the screenshot` MEANS
    REFUSE "the SimpLEX draft's regulation 4 is not visible in the screenshot"

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the SimpLEX draft's regulation 5, commencement, is not visible in the screenshot, and the draft was never in force` MEANS
    REFUSE "the SimpLEX draft's regulation 5, commencement, is not visible in the screenshot, and the draft was never in force"
